### Netcup SCP API — Firewall
# Read and apply firewall state on server interfaces.

### Get Firewall State
# Response: userPolicies, copiedPolicies, ingressImplicitRule, egressImplicitRule, consistent, active
GET {{base_url}}/servers/{{server_id}}/interfaces/{{interface_mac}}/firewall
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}

### Get Firewall State with Consistency Check
# Forces live check — sets 'consistent' to true/false
GET {{base_url}}/servers/{{server_id}}/interfaces/{{interface_mac}}/firewall?consistencyCheck=true
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}

### Apply Firewall Policies (async — returns task UUID)
# userPolicies: array of {"id": N} objects (NOT bare integers)
# copiedPolicies: required field (use [] to clear)
# active: true to enforce, false to disable firewall
PUT {{base_url}}/servers/{{server_id}}/interfaces/{{interface_mac}}/firewall
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "copiedPolicies": [],
  "userPolicies": [{"id": {{policy_id}}}],
  "active": true
}

### Reapply Firewall (async — returns task UUID)
# Use when policy update timed out due to long-running write operation (e.g., storage optimization)
POST {{base_url}}/servers/{{server_id}}/interfaces/{{interface_mac}}/firewall:reapply
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}

### Restore Copied Policies (async — returns task UUID)
POST {{base_url}}/servers/{{server_id}}/interfaces/{{interface_mac}}/firewall:restore-copied-policies
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
